OnVid - Create AI Videos From Text and
Images
Artificial intelligence is changing how creators, marketers and businesses approach video
production. Instead of beginning every project with filming and complex editing, users can now
transform written ideas and existing images into moving visual content with AI.
OnVid is an online AI video platform that supports text to video and image to video creation. It
brings different generative video technologies into one place and gives users a straightforward
way to experiment with social media content, advertising ideas, product visuals and creative
storytelling.
What Is OnVid
OnVid allows users to create AI generated videos from written prompts or images. The process
begins with a description or an existing visual. Users can then choose an available AI video
model and generate the result online.
This approach makes AI video creation accessible to people who want to develop visual ideas
without relying on advanced professional editing software.
Create Videos From Text
Text to video AI uses a written description as the starting point for a new video. A prompt can
include details about the subject, environment, movement, lighting, atmosphere, perspective
and camera direction.
For example, a creator could describe a futuristic sports car travelling through a neon city at
night with cinematic camera movement and reflections on a wet street. The AI model interprets
these details and uses them to generate a visual sequence.
Text based generation can be useful for advertising concepts, short form content, storytelling
and early creative development.
Turn Images Into Moving Content
OnVid also supports image to video AI. Users can begin with a photograph, illustration,
landscape or product image and use AI to introduce movement.
A portrait can become a cinematic shot. A landscape can gain environmental motion and
atmosphere. A product photograph can be transformed into a short promotional concept.
This gives creators another way to reuse existing visual assets without manually animating
every part of an image.
Explore Different AI Video Models
AI video models can have different strengths depending on the type of content being created.
Some may work well with realistic motion while others can be useful for cinematic scenes,
stylized visuals, character movement or multimodal generation.
OnVid provides access to technologies such as Kling 3.0, Seedance 2.0, Google Veo 3.1, FLUX 3
and Hailuo 2.3. Users can also explore technologies associated with Runway, Pika, PixVerse,
Luma and MiniMax.
Having several options in one platform allows users to experiment with different approaches and
choose a model that better fits a particular project.
Creative Uses for AI Video
AI generated video can support many types of digital content. Creators can develop short clips
for social media platforms. Businesses can experiment with product focused visuals and
advertising concepts.
Writers and filmmakers can use generated scenes to explore ideas before larger productions
begin. Marketing teams can test UGC style concepts and different campaign directions. Existing
images can also be transformed into more dynamic visual material.
Why Multiple Models Matter
There is no single AI video model that is ideal for every creative task. Results can vary
depending on the prompt, source image, desired movement and visual style.
Access to multiple models gives users more flexibility. Instead of adapting every idea to one
generation engine, creators can compare different approaches and select a technology that
better matches the intended result.
A New Way to Approach Video Creation
Traditional video production often starts with cameras, recorded footage and editing timelines.
Generative AI introduces another workflow where an idea or image can become the starting
point.
A sentence can become a moving scene. A photograph can gain motion. A product concept can
be visualized before traditional production begins.
By combining text to video AI, image to video AI and multiple generative video technologies,
OnVid provides a flexible way to explore modern AI powered video creation.
